NXR-158|Retained evidence and controlled analyzer detection gates|Verification|Engineering checkpoints shall retain explicitly selected passing logs, manifests and audited unstripped images with bounded hash verification; controlled invalid-memory probes shall demonstrate specific analyzer rejection.|Ignored transient evidence can disappear and passing workloads alone do not show that analyzer failure gates are effective.|Native C# collector rejects traversal, links, overwrite, size/count excess and changed/unlisted/duplicate inputs; round-trip/tamper self-tests pass; ASan, UBSan and Memcheck probes require intended diagnostic plus failure.|Native evidence self-tests, actual controlled-failure gates and final package verification.|NXR-152,NXR-157|XDoc C# Native AOT collector with bounded inputs; probe output captured by shared bounded executor.|No firmware services or RAM; intentionally invalid host probe excluded from ordinary builds.|tools/NexRT.Evidence/Program.cs,cmake/host-tests.cmake,tests/memory_negative.cpp,docs/evidence.rst,docs/host-memory.rst|Hashes support consistency rather than authenticity; retained simulation/host evidence is not board qualification or certification.|tools/NexRT.Evidence/Program.cs,cmake/host-tests.cmake,tests/memory_negative.cpp|tools/NexRT.Evidence/Program.cs,tests/memory_negative.cpp|PartialSourceUnverified
